{
  "_comment": "Source of truth for the WT21 cockpit layout, v3 (2026-10-16, after the second in-sim test). Metres, glTF space: +x is the aircraft LEFT, y up, z forward. Read by make-g1000-interior.mjs (screen + plate quads), scaffold.ps1 (panel.cfg), expand-hide.mjs (analogue instruments hidden by visibility) and panelmap/make_preview_layout.mjs (offline Blender preview). The panel face is at z=9.17; frames and knobs of the removed instruments reach z=9.1513, so plates sit just in front of that.",
  "_comment_plate": "Each unit = a screen quad (the WT21 page, standard 1024x768 / 1024x1024 texture) in front of a plate quad that hides the empty instrument pockets. The plate has a TEXTURED material (F27WT21_PLATE.PNG.DDS, solid dark grey, made by make-plate-dds.mjs): an untextured bezel did not render (test 1) and a dark margin drawn inside a bigger screen texture came out smaller/lower than computed (test 2).",
  "_comment_boxes": "Test 6 (2026-10-16): seen from above (the user's eye), the 2 cm between a plate and the panel face showed the empty pockets above every plate. Plates and the FCP are therefore closed BOXES: four wall quads (the same quad mesh, rotated) run from the front face back to the panel face (panelFaceZ, or the unit's/panel's backZ). Walls use the plain plate material.",
  "_comment_v8": "v8 (user, 2026-10-16: telas com moldura fina 3D, painel de AP e dois DCPs em 3D): real 3D hardware generated as new meshes in the interior's own vertex format (tools/hw3d.mjs, appended to a copy of the interior .bin), one atlas material (tools/make-hw-atlas.py). Displays: thin raised frame, glass recessed 3 mm; the pocket area around is a panel-coloured insert (closed box). FCP and DCPs: CJ4-grey modules with raised key caps and knobs (concentric for MENU/DATA). Controls: rect normalised to the module (x from the pilot's left, y from the top); 'height' = protrusion in metres.",
